---
description: docs/**/*.rst
globs:
alwaysApply: false
---
   1. Use reStructuredText format for all documentation files
    2. Follow these section header markers consistently:
       - = for document title (over and under)
       - - for sections
       - ^ for subsections
       - " for sub-subsections
    3. Include practical examples in code blocks
    4. Use cross-references to link between documents
    5. Keep code examples consistent with the latest version
    6. Include command-line examples with expected output
    7. Document all options and their effects
    8. Use proper indentation for code blocks (3 spaces)
    9. Include troubleshooting sections for common issues
    10. Keep line length under 100 characters
